<h2 id=3D"setting-up-cocos2d-x">Setting up Cocos2d-x<a class=3D"anchorjs-li=
nk " href=3D"https://docs.cocos2d-x.org/cocos2d-x/v4/en/installation/Linux.=
html#setting-up-cocos2d-x" aria-label=3D"Anchor" data-anchorjs-icon=3D"=EE=
=A7=8B" style=3D"font: 1em / 1 anchorjs-icons; padding-left: 0.375em;"></a>=
</h2>
<p>You can get started with <strong>Cocos2d-x</strong> by either downloadin=
g a self-contained <strong>.zip</strong> from the <a href=3D"https://cocos2=
d-x.org/download" target=3D"_blank">website</a> or by cloning our
<a href=3D"https://github.com/cocos2d/cocos2d-x" target=3D"_blank">GitHub R=
epo</a>. Pick what works for you. <strong>There is no need to do both.</str=
ong></p>
<h3 id=3D"by-downloading-a-zip-archive">By downloading a .zip archive<a cla=
ss=3D"anchorjs-link " href=3D"https://docs.cocos2d-x.org/cocos2d-x/v4/en/in=
stallation/Linux.html#by-downloading-a-zip-archive" aria-label=3D"Anchor" d=
ata-anchorjs-icon=3D"=EE=A7=8B" style=3D"font: 1em / 1 anchorjs-icons; padd=
ing-left: 0.375em;"></a></h3>
<p>Download Cocos2d-x and unzip it. (maybe: <strong>~/</strong> or <strong>=
~/Projects</strong> )</p>
<h3 id=3D"cloning-from-github">Cloning from GitHub<a class=3D"anchorjs-link=
 " href=3D"https://docs.cocos2d-x.org/cocos2d-x/v4/en/installation/Linux.ht=
ml#cloning-from-github" aria-label=3D"Anchor" data-anchorjs-icon=3D"=EE=A7=
=8B" style=3D"font: 1em / 1 anchorjs-icons; padding-left: 0.375em;"></a></h=
3>
<p>Use the following commands to clone our GitHub repo and get your environ=
ment setup. If you are not familar with GitHub's workflow, <a href=3D"https=
://guides.github.com/activities/hello-world/" target=3D"_blank">learn it</a=
> or download using the step above, <strong>By downloading a .zip archive</=
strong>.</p>
<h4 id=3D"clone-repo-and-setup-dependencies">Clone Repo and setup dependenc=
ies<a class=3D"anchorjs-link " href=3D"https://docs.cocos2d-x.org/cocos2d-x=
/v4/en/installation/Linux.html#clone-repo-and-setup-dependencies" aria-labe=
l=3D"Anchor" data-anchorjs-icon=3D"=EE=A7=8B" style=3D"font: 1em / 1 anchor=
js-icons; padding-left: 0.375em;"></a></h4>
<pre><code class=3D"lang-sh">// all linux versions
<span class=3D"hljs-built_in">cd</span> &lt;to <span class=3D"hljs-built_in=
">where</span> you want to <span class=3D"hljs-built_in">clone</span> this =
repo&gt;

git <span class=3D"hljs-built_in">clone</span> https://github.com/cocos2d/c=
ocos2d-x.git

<span class=3D"hljs-built_in">cd</span> cocos2d-x-root <span class=3D"hljs-=
comment">#where your cocos2d-x directory is located.</span>

git submodule update --init

git submodule update

// Ubuntu 16, 17
python download-deps.py

// Ubuntu 18, 20
python2 download-deps.py
</code></pre>
<h2 id=3D"make-sure-you-have-a-working-environment">Make sure you have a wo=
rking environment!<a class=3D"anchorjs-link " href=3D"https://docs.cocos2d-=
x.org/cocos2d-x/v4/en/installation/Linux.html#make-sure-you-have-a-working-=
environment" aria-label=3D"Anchor" data-anchorjs-icon=3D"=EE=A7=8B" style=
=3D"font: 1em / 1 anchorjs-icons; padding-left: 0.375em;"></a></h2>
<p>See <strong>Prerequisites</strong> above. This means a working <strong>P=
ython</strong>, <strong>git</strong> and <strong>curl</strong> along with t=
he dependency list above.</p>
<h2 id=3D"building-cocos2d-x">Building Cocos2d-x<a class=3D"anchorjs-link "=
 href=3D"https://docs.cocos2d-x.org/cocos2d-x/v4/en/installation/Linux.html=
#building-cocos2d-x" aria-label=3D"Anchor" data-anchorjs-icon=3D"=EE=A7=8B"=
 style=3D"font: 1em / 1 anchorjs-icons; padding-left: 0.375em;"></a></h2>
<ul>
<li><p>Run <strong>cmake</strong> to generate <strong>makefile</strong>:</p=
>
<pre><code class=3D"lang-sh"><span class=3D"hljs-built_in">cd</span> cocos2=
d-x-root <span class=3D"hljs-comment"># where your cocos2d-x directory is l=
ocated.</span>
mkdir -p build/linux-build
<span class=3D"hljs-built_in">cd</span> build/linux-build
cmake ../..
</code></pre>
</li>
<li><p>When <strong>cmake</strong> finishes, many files &amp; folders will =
be generated in <strong>coocs2dx_root/build/linux-build</strong></p>
<p>  <img src=3D"https://docs.cocos2d-x.org/cocos2d-x/v4/en/installation/Li=
nux-img/1.png" alt=3D""></p>
</li>
<li><p>Run <strong>make</strong> to compile:</p>
<pre><code class=3D"lang-sh">make -j 4
</code></pre>
<p>Everything will be generated in <strong>cocos2dx_root/build/linux-build/=
bin/cpp-tests/</strong>
if compiled successfully.</p>
</li>
<li><p>Run <code>cpp-tests</code></p>
<pre><code class=3D"lang-sh"><span class=3D"hljs-built_in">cd</span> cocos2=
dx_root/build/linux-build/bin/cpp-tests/
./cpp-tests
</code></pre>
</li>
</ul>
<h2 id=3D"starting-a-new-project">Starting a new project<a class=3D"anchorj=
s-link " href=3D"https://docs.cocos2d-x.org/cocos2d-x/v4/en/installation/Li=
nux.html#starting-a-new-project" aria-label=3D"Anchor" data-anchorjs-icon=
=3D"=EE=A7=8B" style=3D"font: 1em / 1 anchorjs-icons; padding-left: 0.375em=
;"></a></h2>
<p>Once everything above works, you can start a new project! To do this, re=
ad our document on the <strong><a href=3D"https://docs.cocos2d-x.org/cocos2=
d-x/v4/en/editors_and_tools/cocosCLTool.html">Cocos Command-line tool</a></=
strong>.</p>
<h2 id=3D"troubleshooting">Troubleshooting<a class=3D"anchorjs-link " href=
=3D"https://docs.cocos2d-x.org/cocos2d-x/v4/en/installation/Linux.html#trou=
bleshooting" aria-label=3D"Anchor" data-anchorjs-icon=3D"=EE=A7=8B" style=
=3D"font: 1em / 1 anchorjs-icons; padding-left: 0.375em;"></a></h2>
<p>Please see this <a href=3D"https://docs.cocos2d-x.org/cocos2d-x/v4/en/fa=
q/linux.html">F.A.Q</a> for troubleshooting help. <strong>Linux</strong> ha=
s a few <strong>known issues.</strong></p>

